{"id":"CVE-2017-7526","state":"PUBLISHED","assigner":"redhat","published":"2018-07-26T13:00:00.000Z","updated":"2025-12-17T22:06:14.998Z","description":"libgcrypt before version 1.7.8 is vulnerable to a cache side-channel attack resulting into a complete break of RSA-1024 while using the left-to-right method for computing the sliding-window expansion. The same attack is believed to work on RSA-2048 with moderately more computation. This side-channel requires that attacker can run arbitrary software on the hardware where the private RSA key is used.","cwe":["CWE-200 CWE-200"],"metrics":[{"src":"cna","v":"3.0","score":6.1,"sev":"MEDIUM","vector":"CVSS:3.0/AV:N/AC:H/PR:N/UI:R/S:C/C:H/I:N/A:N"},{"src":"CISA-ADP","ssvc":{"Exploitation":"none","Automatable":"no","Technical Impact":"partial"}}],"affected":[{"vendor":"GnuPG","product":"libgcrypt","versions":["affected 1.7.8"]}],"references":[{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3733-1/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3733-1"},{"url":"https://bugzilla.redhat.com/show_bug.cgi?id=CVE-2017-7526","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"http://www.securitytracker.com/id/1038915","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_SECTRACK"],"name":"1038915"},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2017/dsa-3960","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-3960"},{"url":"https://git.gnupg.org/cgi-bin/gitweb.cgi?p=libgcrypt.git%3Ba=commit%3Bh=78130828e9a140a9de4dafadbc844dbb64cb709a","tags":["x_refsource_CONFIRM"]},{"url":"https://www.debian.org/security/2017/dsa-3901","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_DEBIAN"],"name":"DSA-3901"},{"url":"https://usn.ubuntu.com/3733-2/","tags":["vendor-advisory","x_refsource_UBUNTU"],"name":"USN-3733-2"},{"url":"https://eprint.iacr.org/2017/627","tags":["x_refsource_MISC"]},{"url":"http://www.securityfocus.com/bid/99338","tags":["vdb-entry","x_refsource_BID"],"name":"99338"},{"url":"https://lists.gnupg.org/pipermail/gnupg-announce/2017q2/000408.html","tags":["mailing-list","